      "score": null,
      "comments": null,
      "author": "Alexander Neubeck",
      "published": "2026-07-31T16:00:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "GitHub achieved ASCII case-folding speeds exceeding 45 GiB/s on a single CPU core for code search.",
        "The technique uses a branch-free loop and byte-space arithmetic to prevent CPU branch mispredictions during text processing.",
        "Processing bytes unconditionally avoids early-exit overhead, saturating memory bandwidth instead of suffering branch misprediction stalls."
      ]
    },
